INSERT INTO imported_classes (class_id, name, system, markdown, status, created_by)
SELECT 'hu-alien-edu-military-specialist', 'Military Specialist (Alien)', 'heroes-unlimited', '---
id: hu-alien-edu-military-specialist
name: "Military Specialist (Alien)"
system: heroes-unlimited
source_book: Revised Heroes Unlimited p.56
category: occ
occ_group: optional
skills:
  occ_skills:
    - { choose: 5, categories: ["Espionage", "Military"], note: "Printed 56: five espionage and/or military skills, from the two categories combined." }
    - { choose: 1, from: ["Hand to Hand: Basic", "Hand to Hand: Expert", "Hand to Hand: Martial Arts"], note: "Printed 56: one hand to hand skill." }
    - { choose: 3, categories: ["Physical"], note: "Printed 56: three physical skills." }
    - { choose: 4, categories: ["Weapon Proficiencies"], note: "Printed 56: four W.P.s. A W.P. has no percentage, so no bonus could apply to these anyway." }
  occ_related_skills: { count: 0 }
  occ_secondary_skills: { count: 4 }
---

## Lore

Rolled 21-40 on the Alien''s own education table, printed 56, STEP FIVE.

**The Alien does not roll on the Educational Level table.** Printed 27 sends every Power Category to that table except Special Training and Physical Training; the Alien goes there too, and then printed 56 prints a five-outcome table of its own that REPLACES it. So this is an occupation in the same slot as the eleven Educational Levels, and the Alien R.C.C. admits these five and nothing else.

Skill bonus: 1D20%, ROLLED, and not applied to secondary skills.

Printed 56: "A skill bonus of 1D20% applies (roll one twenty-sided die for the skill percentile bonus). The bonus does not apply to secondary skills." NO BONUS IS STORED, because it is rolled and a choice group takes a number. Roll 1D20 at creation and add it to every skill above by hand. See BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F83.

Printed 56 closes the table with a rule that belongs to all five: *"All aliens can be taught THREE additional secondary Earth skills, but only if taught by a friendly human."* That is a thing that happens in play rather than at creation, so it is not in the secondary count above.

The Alien''s S.D.C. base of 20, its appearance, its homeworld environment and its powers all belong to the Alien R.C.C. on printed 55-59, not here. This class is the schooling and nothing else.
', 'published', 'data-script'
